{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1784624062,"nonce":"IC+IR/8qWDro5ZndOKErG8Nc2/A=","title":"Shared service — provisioning, reachability \u0026 readiness gate","message":"## Parent\nEpic 01c81a5\n\n## What to build\nThe opt-in Shared form. Pipeline-level `services:` declarations + per-Step `uses: [name]` opt-in. The engine tracks a Run-scoped durable service resource keyed `{run, take}` (eager birth at run start, torn down via namespace-per-run teardown). The executor creates a standalone Pod + k8s Service (DNS `name:\u003cport\u003e`); a network policy scopes reachability to opt-in Pods only. The scheduler holds each opt-in Step until the service readiness probe passes (reuses the probe schema from slice 1). A Rerun's new Take gets a FRESH instance that never sees the prior Take's writes. Governance as in slice 1, keyed on the service image digest. Shared services are unfenced — intra-Take idempotency is a step-author contract (do NOT build fencing for it).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Pipeline-level `services:` + per-Step `uses:` parse + validate\n- [ ] Run-scoped service resource is durable, keyed {run, take}, born at run start, torn down with the run namespace\n- [ ] Executor creates the service Pod + k8s Service; opt-in Step Pods can resolve/reach it by DNS; non-opt-in Pods cannot (network policy)\n- [ ] Scheduler gates opt-in Steps on readiness; ready-timeout fails opt-in Steps fail-closed\n- [ ] A Rerun (new Take) provisions a fresh instance\n- [ ] Tests: two Steps (migrate→test) share one instance across Pods; fresh instance on Rerun\n\n## Blocked by\nSlice 1 (f88a1ab) — reuses the `ready:` probe schema","files":null}]}